# Fiddler — ODS integration analysis

## Executive summary

Fiddler explores CPU/GPU collaborative execution for large MoE models. Instead of using CPU only as a storage tier, selected computation can be performed on CPU to reduce data movement to the GPU.

**ODS classification: P2 research capability.**

## ODS fit

The main contribution is a scheduling decision:

GPU execution versus CPU execution versus transfer cost.

This fits naturally into an ODS execution optimizer that considers hardware, bandwidth, memory pressure and workload characteristics.

Fiddler should currently be treated as research evidence, not a production ODS backend.